.TH F3D-THUMBNAIL-PAIR 1 "17 November 2026" "Sparky Stereo OS"
.SH NAME
f3d-thumbnail-pair \- draw a 3D model as a stereo pair for a file manager's thumbnail
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B f3d-thumbnail-pair
.I PLUGIN SIZE INPUT OUTPUT
.SH DESCRIPTION
Draws the model in
.I INPUT
through libf3d, once for the left eye and once for the right eye (two parallel cameras whose frusta meet at the focal distance), and writes one PNG file,
.I OUTPUT,
of
.I SIZE
by
.I SIZE/2
pixels: the left eye in the left half, the right eye in the right half.
The picture carries the text X\-KDE::Stereo3DLayout=sideBySideLeftFirst, which the file managers of Sparky Stereo OS read; a screen without 3D shows the left half.
.PP
.I PLUGIN
is the F3D plugin that reads the file (native, assimp, occt, draco, hdf) or "all".
The arguments are those of the freedesktop thumbnailer files in /usr/share/thumbnailers (%s, %i and %o).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the picture was written, 1 when the model could not be drawn (the reason is written to the standard error), 2 for a wrong argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR f3d (1)
